('127.671.d.2.D',3,'In https://www.example.com/help, the part ''https'' is the:','["protocol", "file name", "domain name", "port number only"]'::jsonb,0,'The protocol tells how to connect.','original'),
('127.671.d.2.D',4,'In the URL https://www.example.com/help, ''.com'' is part of the:','["file path", "domain name", "query string", "protocol"]'::jsonb,1,'The domain identifies the site.','original'),
('127.671.d.2.E',3,'A student checks who wrote a web article, when it was updated and whether it cites sources. This is testing information for:','["color and layout", "speed and volume", "accuracy and reliability", "price and brand"]'::jsonb,2,'Evaluate before trusting.','original'),
('127.671.d.2.E',4,'Which website is typically the most reliable for a report on health statistics?','["a gaming forum", "an anonymous blog", "a joke site", "a government health agency"]'::jsonb,3,'Official sources are more reliable.','original'),
('127.671.d.2.F',3,'A program that attaches itself to files and spreads when they are opened is a:','["virus", "router", "keyboard", "monitor"]'::jsonb,0,'Viruses spread through files.','original'),
('127.671.d.2.F',4,'Software designed to secretly collect your information without your knowledge is called:','["shareware", "spyware", "freeware", "firmware"]'::jsonb,1,'Spyware records activity.','original'),
('127.671.d.2.G',3,'Someone using your personal data without permission to pose as you is committing:','["routine backup", "file sharing", "identity theft", "screen sharing"]'::jsonb,2,'Protect personal data.','original'),
('127.671.d.2.G',4,'Which habit best protects you from online predators?','["sharing passwords with friends", "posting your address", "meeting strangers alone", "never sharing personal details with strangers"]'::jsonb,3,'Limit what you reveal online.','original'),
('127.671.d.3.A',3,'The part of a computer that carries out instructions is the:','["CPU", "speaker", "monitor", "mouse"]'::jsonb,0,'The CPU processes data.','original'),
('127.671.d.3.A',4,'Temporary memory that is cleared when power is turned off is:','["hard drive", "RAM", "flash storage", "DVD"]'::jsonb,1,'RAM is volatile.','original'),
('127.671.d.3.B',3,'A user looks up a command in the help menu or a manual. This is using a:','["power cord", "game controller", "reference tool", "sound card"]'::jsonb,2,'Reference tools answer questions.','original'),
('127.671.d.3.B',4,'Which is a reference tool for learning how a software feature works?','["the desktop wallpaper", "a random advertisement", "the screen saver", "the built-in help documentation"]'::jsonb,3,'Documentation explains features.','original'),
('127.671.d.3.C',3,'A device you plug in to type text into a computer is a:','["keyboard", "printer", "projector", "scanner"]'::jsonb,0,'Keyboards are input devices.','original'),
('127.671.d.3.C',4,'A microphone is classified as which kind of peripheral?','["power device", "input device", "output device", "storage device"]'::jsonb,1,'It sends sound into the computer.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.A',3,'The software that manages hardware and runs other programs is called:','["a web page", "application software", "system software", "a spreadsheet"]'::jsonb,2,'System software supports the computer.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.A',4,'A word processor and a web browser are examples of:','["hardware", "system software", "firmware", "application software"]'::jsonb,3,'Applications help users do tasks.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.B',3,'Windows, macOS and Linux are examples of:','["operating systems", "web browsers", "search engines", "spreadsheets"]'::jsonb,0,'The OS manages the computer.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.B',4,'Which task is handled by an operating system?','["composing songs", "managing memory and files", "writing essays", "drawing charts"]'::jsonb,1,'The OS manages resources.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.C',3,'The extension .jpg usually shows that a file is a(n):','["video", "spreadsheet", "image", "program"]'::jsonb,2,'Extensions indicate type.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.C',4,'A file ending in .docx is most likely created by a:','["image editor", "music player", "compiler", "word processor"]'::jsonb,3,'Docx is a document format.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.D',3,'Computers store data using which number system?','["binary", "decimal only", "hexadecimal only", "Roman"]'::jsonb,0,'Binary uses 0s and 1s.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.D',4,'The binary number 101 equals what in decimal?','["3", "5", "4", "6"]'::jsonb,1,'1x4 + 0x2 + 1x1 = 5.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.E',3,'Software whose source code is freely available for anyone to view and modify is:','["encrypted", "pirated", "open source", "proprietary"]'::jsonb,2,'Open source shares code.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.E',4,'Software owned by a company that restricts access to its source code is called:','["free of license", "open source", "public domain", "proprietary"]'::jsonb,3,'Owners control the code.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.F',3,'A utility that checks a drive for errors and frees up space is a system:','["management tool", "video game", "chat room", "browser plugin"]'::jsonb,0,'These tools maintain the system.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.F',4,'Which system tool removes unneeded temporary files to free space?','["clock", "disk cleanup", "screen saver", "calculator"]'::jsonb,1,'It clears junk files.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.G',3,'Putting related documents into labeled folders is an example of:','["file corruption", "file loss", "file organization", "file damage"]'::jsonb,2,'Folders keep files orderly.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.G',4,'Which file name is best for a May 2025 budget report?','["asdf", "stuff", "new1", "budget_report_2025_05"]'::jsonb,3,'Clear names help you find files.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.H',3,'A secret code used to protect an account from unauthorized access is a:','["password", "font", "cursor", "theme"]'::jsonb,0,'Passwords protect accounts.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.H',4,'Which password is the strongest?','["password", "T7#mQ9!vLp2x", "12345", "qwerty"]'::jsonb,1,'Length and variety make it strong.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.I',3,'When antivirus software finds an infected file, it can place it in:','["the desktop", "the recycle chute", "quarantine", "the cloud"]'::jsonb,2,'Quarantine isolates threats.','original'),
('127.671.d.4.I',4,'After a virus is isolated, the next step is to:','["rename it", "share it", "ignore it", "remove it and update the antivirus"]'::jsonb,3,'Removal prevents damage.','original'),
('127.671.d.5.A',3,'A device that connects networks and directs data packets is a:','["router", "monitor", "speaker", "scanner"]'::jsonb,0,'Routers send data between networks.','original'),
('127.671.d.5.A',4,'A network interface card (NIC) allows a computer to:','["clean files", "connect to a network", "print pages", "store power"]'::jsonb,1,'NICs provide network access.','original'),
('127.671.d.5.B',3,'A network that covers a single building or campus is a:','["wide area network", "personal sound system", "local area network", "global switch"]'::jsonb,2,'LANs are small-scale.','original'),
('127.671.d.5.B',4,'The internet is an example of a:','["personal area network", "closed circuit", "local area network", "wide area network"]'::jsonb,3,'WANs span large distances.','original'),
